    "result_text": "Done. The full build passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 tests green).\n\n## Summary of changes\n\nI redesigned the owner identity key to `SHA-256 hex over (normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName))` and reworked duplicate detection around it.\n\n**New file**\n- `rest/function/common/Soundex.java` \u2014 standard American Soundex encoding (`first letter + 3 digits`), used to fold last names phonetically.\n\n**Identity key** (`OwnerIdentityKey.java`)\n- Now returns the full lowercase 64-char SHA-256 hex over `canonicalTelephone (E.164) | lowerEmail | soundex(lastName)` via the existing `Sha256.hex`. Previously it was a plain pipe string using `householdId`.\n\n**Hard duplicate / 409** (`EnsureUniqueOwnerIdentity.java`)\n- Now rejects with 409 only when the request's whole `identityKey` equals an existing **non-deleted** owner's. Removed the householdId-based block and the `sharesHousehold` bypass. Two owners with same last name + postcode but **different telephones** now have different keys \u2192 not a hard duplicate.\n- Wired into `owners.POST.yml` as a new `ensureUniqueIdentity` step right after `validate`, so the email-domain blocklist (applied in validation) still runs first. This step was previously dead code (never wired).\n\n**Soft match** (`AssignOwnerPossibleDuplicate.java`)\n- Now flags a possible duplicate when the `identityKey` **differs** but `soundex(lastName)` and exact postcode **match** (ignoring self and soft-deleted owners). Replaces the old exact-lastName + household-exclusion logic.\n\n**Supporting updates**\n- `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException` message now references the identity key (409 handler already returned `{\"errors\":[\"identityKey\"]}`).\n- `openapi.yml` descriptions for `identityKey`, `possibleDuplicate`, `possibleDuplicateOf`, and `sharesHousehold` (now inert, retained for compatibility) updated to match; Javadoc across the touched classes updated.\n\nThe `householdId` itself is unchanged and still drives household size and membership level; only the separate household-duplicate 409 block was removed.",
